# internal/scripts/pentest is go:embed'd verbatim into the guardpipe binary
# and then run byte-for-byte as POSIX sh inside the Linux pentest-sandbox
# container. A CRLF checkout (core.autocrlf=true on Windows, the default for
# many contributors) silently corrupts every line here — "$(dirname "$0")"
# resolving to a path with a trailing \r, "not found" sourcing common.sh —
# which fails instantly and identically across every script (naabu, nmap,
# nuclei, ...), well before any tool-specific logic runs. Forcing LF here
# regardless of checkout platform is what actually fixes it; see
# PROGRESS-LOG.md for the incident this line-ending bug caused.
internal/scripts/pentest/** text eol=lf
